 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T07:01+08:00",
 "answer": "They may be showing **different air-quality scales or time windows**—so “moderate” and “unhealthy” aren’t necessarily contradictory.\n\nIf by **PSI** you mean Singapore’s Pollutant Standards Index, its **24-hour** reading is “Moderate” from 51–100 and “Unhealthy” from 101–200. Another app might show a shorter-term reading, focus on PM2.5, or use a different country’s AQI scale; Singapore’s PSI and the U.S. AQI, for example, aren’t identical. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/others/haze/?utm_source=openai))\n\nCheck whether both readings are for the same location and time, and whether the app says **“Unhealthy”** or **“Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups.”** If you tell me which app and PSI source you’re comparing, I can help pinpoint the difference.",
